! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.4, "MODIFIED TRAPEZOIDAL RULE", Method 1, "Create a
! summing loop with the f(xk) evaluation inside the loop", printed p.28
! (PDF 29), read in the ink.
!
!   "Evaluate the integral I = INTEGRAL(0..2) x**4 dx by the modified
!   trapezoidal rule
!     INTEGRAL(a..b) f(x) dx ~ h [ f(a+h/2) + f(a+3h/2) + ... +
!     f(a+nh-h/2) ]  where h = (b-a)/n.  Use n = 20 for this purpose."
!
!       MTZR    LX, $1, XW1
!               L(U), B
!               -(N), A
!               /(N), N
!               ST(U), H
!               E-I(U), 1               'or 128.0
!               +(N), A
!               B, STOR
!       LOOP    L(U), TEMP
!               +(N), H
!       STOR    ST(U), TEMP             'update temp
!               *(N), 8.0               'or $L
!               *(N), 8.0               'new integrand value
!               M+(N), ANS
!               CB, $1, LOOP
!               *(N), H
!               BEW, $
!       XW1     XW, 0.0, 20, $
!       A       DD(N), 0.0              'lower limit
!       B       DD(N), 2.0              'upper limit
!       N       DD(N), 20.0             'no. of strips
!       ANS     DD(N), 0
!       TEMP    DR(N), (1)
!       H       DR(N), (1)
!
! THE WHOLE DECK IS THE PAGE: twenty-four statements, as printed, data
! and all.  The five printed remarks are in this header and not on the
! cards.  Nothing is the deck's but END.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2 (the host STRAP II): strap_asm.py refuses
! "DD(N), 0.0" and "DD(N), 0" (decks/problem_3_dd_zero_fraction.strap).
!
! >>> THE PRINTED PROGRAM DOES NOT FORM THE INTEGRAL. <<<
! "M+(N), ANS" is ADD TO MEMORY: Reference Manual printed p.88-89, "The
! exponent and fraction of the sum replace bits 0-59 of the storage
! word ... The contents of the entire accumulator and its sign byte
! register remain unchanged throughout the operation".  So after the
! loop the accumulator still holds the LAST integrand value, f(x20) =
! 1.95**4, and the page's closing "*(N), H" multiplies that by h, not
! the sum.  ANS holds the sum of the twenty integrand values, never
! multiplied by h; the accumulator ends holding 1.95**4 x 0.1 = 1.4459,
! which is nothing.  The integral the page asks for, 6.38667 (the rule's
! value; the true integral is 6.4), is in neither place.  An "L(U), ANS"
! before the last multiply is what the page lacks.  Method 2 (printed
! pp.28-29) has the same ending.
! THE DECK RUNS THE PAGE AS PRINTED and the checks say what the printed
! program leaves, with the model doing what the manual says:
!
!   ANS       00CFF7786C2265B0   63.866724999991...  the sum of f
!   TEMP      002F999999999900   1.9499999999999...  x20
!   H         007CCCCCCCCCCCD0   0.1000000000000000  h
!   acc_left  002B913458CD1EC0   1.44590062499978    f(x20) x h
!   B_as_assembled 002FFFFFFFFFFFF0,  N_as_assembled 00A9FFFFFFFFFFF0
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE DERIVED FROM THE MANUAL'S RULES, NOT FROM THE
! MODEL, by tests/problem_3_expected.py (p34), because sixty truncating
! steps on 48-bit fractions are not paper work.  The rules it applies
! and their pages are in its header: every "+", "*" and "/" forms its
! exact result and keeps the leading 48 bits (truncation, printed p.80
! and p.86-87, 92, 93-94); M+ does the same into storage; E-I(U), 1
! takes one from the exponent (printed p.102-103); "*(N), 8.0" squares
! the accumulator (C22-6578 printed p.28 comment (b): address 8.0
! "means the leading 60 bits of the accumulator plus the lowest
! four-bits of $SB").
!
! WHAT CAN BE SAID WITHOUT THE CALCULATOR, as a check on it:
!   In exact arithmetic h = 1/10, x(i) = (2i - 1)/20, the sum of
!   x(i)**4 for i = 1..20 is 63.866725 (= 10,218,676 / 160,000:
!   SUM of (2i-1)**4 for i = 1..20 is 10,218,676), and 1.95**4 / 10 =
!   1.445900625.  The words above are those numbers short by a few
!   parts in 10**13, the direction truncation errs.
!   H by hand: 2.0 arrives as 2 - 2**-47 and 20.0 as 20 - 2**-43
!   (below).  (2 - 2**-47)/(20 - 2**-43) = 0.1 x (1 - 2**-48) /
!   (1 - 2**-43/20) = 0.1 x (1 + 0.30 x 2**-47), which is above 0.1 by
!   0.48 of a unit of the 48th place of a number with exponent -3
!   (2**-51).  0.1 is .CCCCCCCCCCCC|CCC... x 2**-3, 0.8 of a unit beyond
!   the 48th place; 0.8 + 0.48 carries, so the truncated fraction is
!   CCCCCCCCCCCD: H = 007CCCCCCCCCCCD0.
!
! THE DECIMAL CONSTANTS.  The host STRAP II converts "2.0" as 20 x a
! truncated 1/10 and "20.0" as 200 x the same, so each is one unit of
! its 48th place short (tests/check_strap2_dd.py; "No printed word
! decides this").  The two input checks pin what was actually loaded,
! so the derivation's premise is itself tested.  With exact 2 and 20
! the calculator gives the same ANS, TEMP and acc_left and H one unit
! lower (007CCCCCCCCCCCC0): the truncations absorb the difference.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): "B DD(N), 2.0" changed to "B DD(N), 3.0".
! FAIL ANS, TEMP, H, acc_left and B_as_assembled; N_as_assembled and the
! PC passed.

MTZR    LX, $1, XW1
        L(U), B
        -(N), A
        /(N), N
        ST(U), H
        E-I(U), 1
        +(N), A
        B, STOR
LOOP    L(U), TEMP
        +(N), H
STOR    ST(U), TEMP
        *(N), 8.0
        *(N), 8.0
        M+(N), ANS
        CB, $1, LOOP
        *(N), H
        BEW, $
XW1     XW, 0.0, 20, $
A       DD(N), 0.0
B       DD(N), 2.0
N       DD(N), 20.0
ANS     DD(N), 0
TEMP    DR(N), (1)
H       DR(N), (1)
        END, MTZR
